{"command":"cd ~/projets/media-workspace/newznab-tmux && git push -q -u origin perf/hopeless-singleton-purge-20261005 2>&1 | tail -2; gh pr create --base microservices-pods --head perf/hopeless-singleton-purge-20261005 --title "perf(releases): early timeout for hopeless single-part collections" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Why

A read-only diagnostic of parked collections (filecheck=1, 1-in-20 sample) found 8,923 of 8,991 in `alt.binaries.hdtv.x264`. Every one is a single binary holding one part of a file that claims 6,655 or 967,646 parts. Those are per-article obfuscated posts: each article has its own random subject and poster, so it becomes its own collection and nothing can join it later. The missed_parts queue is empty.

About 178k of these wait out the full 96h `collection_timeout`. They keep the backlog (~546k) above the orchestrator's HIGH watermark (220k), which pauses backfill and denies current-forward permits.

## What

A new stage, `processHopelessSingletonCollections`, runs right after the stuck-collection cleanup. It deletes a collection only when all of these hold:

- filecheck is 0 or 1, `releases_id` is null, and `totalfiles <= 1`;
- it has exactly one binary;
- `currentparts <= 1`, and the `parts` table also holds at most 1 row for it, so a lagging `currentparts` cannot trigger a delete;
- `totalparts >= NNTMUX_RELEASE_HOPELESS_SINGLETON_MIN_PARTS` (default 50);
- `dateadded` is older than `NNTMUX_RELEASE_HOPELESS_SINGLETON_AGE_HOURS`.

The age defaults to **0, which disables the stage**. Cooperative slices scan one page per group behind a persisted cursor (key `hopeless`). It cannot overlap the split-collection reconciler, which only acts on complete binaries.

## Tests

- New `ReleaseProcessingHopelessSingletonTest`: a full pass, disabled by default, group scope, and the same scenario on MariaDB 11.8. 4/4 pass.
- These suites pass: ReleaseProcessing*, SplitCollectionReconciler, SplitPostingRepair, BraceTokenRepair, ReleaseDeletionCollectionCleanup, CollectionSplitDiagnostics, ReleasesRunner, Unit/Releases and Unit/Binaries.
- The only failure is `test_delayed_collection_is_not_forced_complete_when_any_binary_is_incomplete`, which fails identically on the base.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

https://claude.ai/code/session_01RW6F7nsyE1gb3tKtnvs5xQ
EOF
)"","exitCode":0,"success":true}

