{"command":"gh -R krickwix/newznab-tmux pr create --base microservices-pods --head feat/hopeless-purge-worker-20261009 --title "feat(cleanup): dedicated lane for hopeless single-part collections" --body-file - <<'EOF'
## Why

alt.binaries.boneless adds ~400k collections an hour. A profile of its newest and oldest 20k collections showed 98% are one part of a many-part file from per-article obfuscated posts. The release worker deletes these as one 2,000-row page per slice, and only after 6 hours. It fell behind by two orders of magnitude: the backlog reached 1.3M, orchestrator pressure stayed HIGH, and every backfill stopped.

## What

- `HopelessCollectionPurger` holds the hopeless test, moved out of `ReleaseProcessingService` unchanged. The release stage now calls it.
- `nntmux:purge-hopeless-collections` runs the test over every group in 20k-row pages until its deadline (240s by default). It keeps its cursor in the cache and wraps once per run.
- The new distributed lane `hopeless-purge` runs that command. It is enabled by `NNTMUX_HOPELESS_PURGE_AGE_MINUTES`; 0, the default, turns it off.
  - Tuning settings: `NNTMUX_HOPELESS_PURGE_WINDOW`, `_DEADLINE_SECONDS` and `_SLEEP_SECONDS`.
- Telemetry: `nntmux_worker_items_total{worker="hopeless-purge",item="collection",result="scanned|deleted"}`.

The test is unchanged. A collection matches only if all of these hold:
- one binary;
- one part present;
- at least `min_parts` parts claimed;
- no release;
- older than the cutoff.

Real posts gather their parts within minutes, so they never match.

## Tests

- New tests:
  - the command applies the same scenario as the release stage;
  - its own shorter age applies;
  - the cursor resumes and wraps once;
  - the lane is off at age 0;
  - the lane resolves in the job catalog.
- Results for the files touched: the hopeless, catalog and Prometheus suites pass.
- Unit and feature suites: the same failures as `microservices-pods` with this change applied. These are stale pinned-image manifest assertions plus deobfuscation, NZB-backlog and movie tests, all already failing on the base.

